Careful: negative nanos? modulo works for negative too (hours before 1970 aligned if nanos % HOUR == 0; Java % on negative: -3600e9 % 3600e9 == 0 fine).

windowHours:
```java
static List<Long> windowHours(long startNanos, long endNanos) {
    List<Long> hours = new ArrayList<>();
    long first = Math.floorDiv(startNanos, HOUR_NANOS) * HOUR_NANOS;
    for (long h = first; h < endNanos; h += HOUR_NANOS) hours.add(h);
    return hours;
}
